{
 "schema_version": "1.0.0",
 "note": "Per-episode archive-title queries. The unattended queue used ONE generic list for every episode (prison / jail / police / courtroom ...), which is why a British Post Office IT scandal ended up carrying American patrol footage, a neon HOTEL sign and a rice paddy: the generic terms matched, the subject did not. Each episode now asks for what its own story contains.",
 "episodes": {
  "surfside": {
   "note": "Champlain Towers South, Surfside FL, June 2021: a 12-storey oceanfront condo collapses at 1:22am. 2018 engineer report on garage/pool-deck damage, years of board fights over the repair bill, 98 dead. BANNED SUBJECT MATTER (design owner, 2026-08-02, binding): this film does NOT depict the collapse, the rubble, rescue or firefighting operations, ambulances, casualties or memorial-of-the-dead imagery. The queries debris / demolition / excavator / emergency / ambulance / burning candle / smoke building / abandoned building were removed on that ground and must not come back. The pool is the BUILDING and the DECISION: concrete, columns, the garage, the pool deck, water, balconies, corridors, drawings, meetings, letters and money, the ocean and the night.",
   "_why": "Terms are ANDed SUBSTRING matches against human-written archive titles, so every query here was probed against the ledger before it was written (2026-08-02). The previous list was written as descriptive phrases -- apartment building exterior, cracked concrete, rebar rust corrosion, memorial flowers fence, missing person poster, board meeting -- and 37 of its 38 queries returned ZERO rows. Do not add bare broad words either: rust matches frustrated, surf matches surface, ski matches asking, pier matches copier, sea wall matches wallpaper. The archive has no courtroom, gavel, judge, invoice, envelope or corrosion footage left that another episode has not already taken. Subtropical coastal only: nothing that invites snow, alps, ski, winter, neon sci-fi tunnels or foreign landmarks.",
