  "hyatt": {
   "note": "EP69 Kansas City Hyatt Regency walkways, 1978-1988 USA. Registers R1-R20 and the terms themselves come from the episode's own measured plan, EP69_hyatt_FOOTAGE_PLAN.v001.md s4: each term is one the plan measured a USABLE count for after licence, title-block, rip-signature, on-disk, size, cross-episode and 1920x1080 screens -- not a director's phrase. Five terms the plan measured as actively misleading are deliberately ABSENT even though their hit counts are high: 'plant' (89, botany), 'rig' (60, the word 'bright'), 'nut' (27, doughnuts; top hit is a police clip and 'police' is forbidden), 'cine' (62, 'medicine'/'cinematic') and 'sign' (270, signage carries readable text that places the shot elsewhere). 'people' (410) and 'architect' (424) are also absent: the first floods the people lane with modern crowds and the second returns European civic architecture, which s6 rule 7 bars. NO QUERY TERM IS A forbidden_subjects WORD -- check_spec_satisfied matches those word-wise against the staged FILENAME, so a title carrying collapse/rubble/rescue/police/child/hyatt is an automatic build failure, and this episode is a structural-collapse case where reaching for that imagery is exactly the defamatory cut (EP60 surfside staged 31 of them). Period is the binding risk and no machine measures it: era_setting is 1978-1988 and the steel, drafting and construction registers on this shelf are dominated by 2015-2024 footage, so footage_review_required is true and every clip is judged on frames before it is copied.",
